From 051699c0435e2243bdd6e19d04eed380d197f2b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hfatehi <trialoftheniku@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:44:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] ARCPID: per-radiator correlated term; cards calibration
 v3 (cell-averaged, PDE-sampled full sim)

- ARCPID: GasSigmaCorrFormula / AerogelSigmaCorrFormula, a per-track angular term that does not
  average down with N_pe (optics bias that depends on the position in the cell), added in
  quadrature to sigma_1/sqrt(N_pe); default 0.
- cards (v3): calibrated on a theta-uniform full sim analysed in whole-cell theta bins, with
  each photon kept with probability PDE (the earlier tables weighted photons by PDE, which
  underestimates the per-track sigma by ~0.7, and sampled one position per cell).
  Per-photon resolution = pixel (+) emission (chromatic computed by the module), correlated term,
  yield scale and ring efficiency as even polynomials in cot(theta) (barrel) / tan(theta) (endcap),
  held inside the fitted range; measured constants in the barrel-endcap gap (39.3-44.2 deg).
  N_sat gas 10.43 (L_ref 15 cm), aerogel 6.94 (1 cm); BendingCoefficient 0.155.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KP5vqAGH2XiGXWtPhaonke
